---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Getting Started with Airlock">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Getting started</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 max-w-2xl">
                Install the Airlock Mobile Approver, create your account, pick a
                plan, then pair your IDE or automation tools so approvals reach your
                phone.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-2 mb-4">1. Download the app</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Install <strong class="text-foreground">Airlock Approver</strong> on
                your phone. Store listings will be linked here when available.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-muted-foreground list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Apple App Store</strong> —
                    coming soon
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Google Play</strong> — coming
                    soon
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">
                2. Create an Airlock account
            </h2>
            <ol class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground list-decimal pl-5">
                <li>Open the Airlock Approver app.</li>
                <li>
                    Sign in with <strong class="text-foreground">Google</strong>,
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Apple</strong>, or
                    <strong class="text-foreground">GitHub</strong> (browser-based
                    OIDC), or use <strong class="text-foreground">Create Account</strong>
                    for email registration on the login screen.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">
                3. Subscription and plans
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-muted-foreground list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                    New accounts are assigned the
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Free</strong> plan automatically
                    (default subscription on registration).
                </li>
                <li>
                    To change your plan, open
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Settings</strong> in the app
                    (gear icon on the Workspaces screen).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Under the <strong class="text-foreground">SUBSCRIPTION</strong>
                    section, you will see your current plan, workspace limit, and
                    monthly approval usage. Tap that card to open the upgrade screen
                    and choose a plan that fits your budget and usage.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4">
                On the Free plan, adding a second workspace opens the subscription
                flow when you tap
                <strong class="text-foreground">Pair Another Workspace</strong>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">
                4. Install an enforcer (before pairing)
            </h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Before pairing, install the Host Enforcer that matches where your AI
                agent runs. The mobile app completes pairing by scanning a QR code
                or entering a 6-character code shown by the enforcer.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-muted-foreground list-disc pl-5 mt-3">
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/claude-code" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Claude Code</a
                    >
                    — plugin and pairing commands
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/cursor" class="text-link hover:underline">Cursor</a>,
                    <a href="/docs/windsurf" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Windsurf</a
                    >,
                    <a href="/docs/antigravity" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Antigravity</a
                    >,
                    <a href="/docs/copilot" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >GitHub Copilot</a
                    >
                    — VS Code–style extensions
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/cli" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Airlock CLI</a
                    >
                    and
                    <a href="/docs/shells" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >shell plugins</a
                    >
                    — terminal workflows
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/n8n" class="text-link hover:underline">n8n</a> —
                    workflow automation nodes
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/developer-guide" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Developer guide</a
                    >
                    — custom apps and Gateway integration
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">5. Pair your workspace</h2>
            <ol class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground list-decimal pl-5">
                <li>
                    After you sign in, the app walks you through
                    <strong class="text-foreground">initial pairing</strong> if you
                    have not paired a workspace yet (QR scan or enter code). When you
                    already have a pairing, the home screen is
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Workspaces</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    From <strong class="text-foreground">Workspaces</strong>, open
                    pairings in either way:
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
                        <li>
                            Tap the <strong class="text-foreground">settings</strong> icon
                            (top left), then <strong class="text-foreground"
                                >Workspace Pairings</strong
                            >, or
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Tap the floating action button (link icon) at the bottom —
                            tooltip <strong class="text-foreground"
                                >Workspace Pairings</strong
                            >.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    On <strong class="text-foreground">Workspace Pairings</strong>,
                    tap <strong class="text-foreground">Pair Another Workspace</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Choose <strong class="text-foreground">Scan QR</strong> or
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Enter Code</strong> (segmented
                    control on the pairing screen). Scan the QR shown by your enforcer,
                    or type the 6-character pairing code.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Claude Code</strong> typically
                    shows a text pairing code — use
                    <strong class="text-foreground">Enter Code</strong> and submit.
                </li>
                <li>
                    For <strong class="text-foreground">n8n</strong>, follow the
                    workflow and credential steps in the
                    <a href="/docs/n8n" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >n8n integration guide</a
                    >.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline">← All Docs</a>
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to Airlock</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
